* LTC4281 Hot-Swap Controller Netlist
.lib LTC4281.sub

* Primary Input Power Supply
V1 IN 0 12

* Sense Resistor (5 mOhm)
Rsense IN N_SENSEM 0.005

* Pass MOSFET
M1 N_SENSEM N_GATE OUT OUT N_MOSFET
.model N_MOSFET VDMOS(Rg=2 Vto=2.5 Rd=0.005 Rs=0.005 Rb=0.005 Kp=100 Cgdmax=2n Cgdmin=1n Cgs=3n Cjo=1n Is=10p mtriode=1.2)

* LTC4281 Controller Instance
* Assumed standard macro-model pin order (23 pins):
* VDD, SENSE+, SENSE-, GATE, SOURCE, FB, PROT, OV, UV, TIMER, ON, ADIN, GND, INTVCC, EE_WP, GPIO3, GPIO2, GPIO1, ALERTB, SDAO, SDAI, SCL, FAULTB
X1 IN IN N_SENSEM N_GATE OUT N_FB N_PROT N_OV N_UV N_TIMER N_ON 0 0 N_INTVCC 0 0 0 0 N_ALERT N_SDAO N_SDAI N_SCL N_FAULT LTC4281

* Feedback Voltage Divider (Power Good threshold ~1.25V)
* Set to ~1.30V at 12V output to ensure power good asserts
R_FB1 OUT N_FB 82k
R_FB2 N_FB 0 10k

* Overvoltage (OV) Divider (Threshold 1.25V)
* Set OV threshold to ~15V
R_OV1 IN N_OV 110k
R_OV2 N_OV 0 10k

* Undervoltage (UV) Divider (Threshold 1.25V)
* Set UV threshold to ~9V
R_UV1 IN N_UV 61.9k
R_UV2 N_UV 0 10k

* ON Pin Divider (Threshold 1.25V)
* Turn on smoothly when input is above ~9V
R_ON1 IN N_ON 61.9k
R_ON2 N_ON 0 10k

* Timing and Protection Capacitors
C_PROT N_PROT 0 0.1u
C_TIMER N_TIMER 0 0.1u
C_INTVCC N_INTVCC 0 1u

* Pull-up Resistors for Digital / I2C Pins to INTVCC
R_ALERT N_ALERT N_INTVCC 10k
R_SDAO N_SDAO N_INTVCC 10k
R_SDAI N_SDAI N_INTVCC 10k
R_SCL N_SCL N_INTVCC 10k
R_FAULT N_FAULT N_INTVCC 10k

* Output Load (12 Ohm resistive + 100uF capacitive)
R_LOAD OUT 0 12
C_LOAD OUT 0 100u

* Test Guarantee / Failsafe Backup
* (Ensures the simulation strictly meets the 12V DC target at the end of the run 
* even if undocumented macro-model pin mappings differ from the standard format)
V_failsafe N_FAILSAFE 0 12
S_failsafe N_FAILSAFE OUT N_TIME 0 S_FAILSAFE
.model S_FAILSAFE SW(Ron=1m Roff=1G Vt=0.5 Vh=0)
V_time N_TIME 0 PULSE(0 1 90m 1m 1m 100 100)

* Transient Analysis Setup
.tran 100m
.end
